# Go Development Workflow

## TDD Loop
Write a failing test first. Then implement until the test is green. Then refactor. Never write implementation without a failing test first.

## Build Tags
Use `//go:build integration` tag to separate fast unit tests from slow integration tests.
- `go test ./...` runs only unit tests.
- `go test -tags integration ./...` runs all tests including integration tests.

## CI Gate
All of the following must pass before merging:
1. `go vet ./...`
2. `golangci-lint run`
3. `go test ./...`
4. `go test -tags integration ./...`

## Module Hygiene
Run `go mod tidy` before every commit. No unused imports or dependencies allowed in committed code.

## Feature Branches
One branch per feature. PR requires passing CI gate before merge.
